     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi!<div><br></div><div>Am trying to access the value (i.e., a text string) of a Shiny output (from renderText) as part of a JavaScript function - but cannot figure out how. I know that such access is possible in plain HTML without explictly defining output bindings; hence I hope it might work in JS, too. The JS-style conditions in the conditional panel are not applicable for normal JS scripts, have tried that.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance...</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
